Tomcat Integration & Configuration:

Tomcat Installation:
	[] yum install java-1.8.0-openjdk-devel -y
	[] wget https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.120/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.120.tar.gz
	[] tar -xvzf apache-tomcat-9.0.120.tar.gz
	[] cd apache-tomcat-9.0.120
	[] ls -latr
	[] cd conf/
-> Add below lines in tomcatusers.xml
	[] vi tomcatusers.xml
	<role rolename=”manager-gui”/>
	<role rolename=”manager-script”/>
	<user username=”tomcat” password=”tomcat” roles=”manager-script,manager-gui”/>
-> After adding above lines save the file
-> Navigate to apache-tomcat-9.0.120/webapps/manager/META-INF
	[] vi context.xml
-> Comment the below line
	<!--
	  <Valve className="org.apache.catalina.valves.RemoteAddrValve"
	        allow="127\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|::1|0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1" />
	-->
-> Save the file and exit.
-> Start the tomcat 
	[] cd apache-tomcat-9.0.120/bin
	[] ./startup.sh
-> Here tomcat will start 
-> Hit the browser with PubIP:8080
-> Click on manager app and login with credentials.

Configuring Job:
-> Go to Jenkins UI > Install the Deploy to Container plugin.
-> Go to Build → Source Code Management → Select Git → Provide the Repository URL → Click on build steps > Invoke top-level Maven targets > Provide the Maven version and set the goal as install -DskipTests > Click on Post build follow this
	[] WAR/EAR File: **/*.war
	[] Content Path: Where we gonna Store
-> Add Credentials > Click On Username and Password
	Username: tomcat
	Password: tomcat
	ID: Tomcat > Create
	Tomcat URL: PubIP:8080 > Save
